Created all four files in `design/brand/kiro/`:

- **kiro-icon.svg** — replaces the thin 4.6-unit stroked V with a filled path (~7.6-unit visual weight), rounded apex instead of a sharp vertex, fork tines sitting directly on the left leg's shoulder, and an enlarged spoon bowl pulled clear of the radar arc.
- **kiro-favicon.svg** — 32×32 variant that keeps only the heavy V, a simplified single-ellipse spoon, a thinner arc (1.7 units) and the discovery dot, dropping the fork's double-tine detail for small-size clarity.
- **kiro-mark.svg** — transparent standalone version with the same geometry in charcoal ink, gold reserved for the single discovery point.
- **design-notes.md** — Chinese write-up covering the V's filled-path construction, apex rounding, shoulder/visual-weight measurements, and spacing rationale; credits Claude Sonnet 5 via Kiro CLI.

All three new SVGs reuse the existing arc sweep, canvas, and color values from the reference files so the three-way comparison stays apples-to-apples.
